# Channels: a channel's episodes are films. The finished film, its source, its stills and its credits go to
# GitHub. Render outputs and generated speech stay local — build.sh regenerates them.
# (The same rules as films/.gitignore: a channel's episodes are films, only deeper.)

# Render outputs (segments, video-only mux, mixes)
**/out/

# Generated speech and music (TTS lines, processed chunks, score renders) — the scripts next to them are kept
**/*.wav
**/*.mp3

# Oversized intermediate WAVs (the mixed track, hundreds of MB) never enter git
**/mix.wav

# The speech cache, the scratch pages and the render locks stay local
**/voice/.cache/
**/test/
**/scratch/
**/*.lock

# Episodes stay on this machine (finished films run to hundreds of MB, past what GitHub takes)
**/*.mp4
*/series/_*/

# The Trạm Nghĩ Nhiều episodes stay on this machine entirely — the whole series folder is ignored, not
# just its renders and its films. The episodes that were already in the index were taken out of it
# (git rm --cached), so the index does not grow with a hundred review files and a finished film per
# episode. The work is not lost: it stays in this working tree and in the history of this repository.
tram-nghi-nhieu/series/

